h+='<div style="margin-top:10px;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(99,102,241,.04);border-left:3px solid #6366f1;font-size:9px;color:var(--text2);line-height:1.7"><strong style="color:#6366f1">💡 In simple terms:</strong> This compares how the business is doing (earnings growth) vs how the stock is doing (price change). When both move in the same direction, the market is rational. When earnings are up but price is down (like MU in 2024), the market is worried about something the balance sheet doesn\'t show yet — forward guidance, competition, or macro risk. When earnings are down but price is up, the market is betting on a turnaround that hasn\'t happened yet — risky.</div>';
