h+='<div style="margin-top:10px;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(99,102,241,.04);border-left:3px solid #6366f1;font-size:9px;color:var(--text2);line-height:1.7"><strong style="color:#6366f1">💡 In simple terms:</strong> These are the headlines driving sentiment. '+(_bCats>_gCats?'News is predominantly negative ('+_bCats+' bearish vs '+_gCats+' bullish) — the market is reacting to bad news or uncertainty. Stocks often overshoot on negative sentiment, creating opportunities for patient investors if the business is strong.':_gCats>_bCats?'News flow is positive ('+_gCats+' bullish vs '+_bCats+' bearish) — sentiment is supportive.':'News is mixed — no clear narrative direction. The stock is waiting for a catalyst.')+'</div>';
